Summary:
focused on revising the previously learned MongoDB concepts and queries. We reviewed the fundamentals of MongoDB, including databases, collections, documents, and basic query syntax. Special attention was given to revisiting CRUD operations and understanding how each operation works in managing database records. The revision helped reinforce the practical knowledge gained in earlier sessions.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, we strengthened our understanding of MongoDB fundamentals and basic queries. The revision improved our confidence in performing CRUD operations such as inserting, retrieving, updating, and deleting documents. This helped build a stronger foundation for working with MongoDB in real-world applications. 
